{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00185",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 3.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Evening. Long day, I imagine. Sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.72,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 6.83,
      "end_seconds": 12.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "So, hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.21,
      "end_seconds": 14.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Was parking alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.85,
      "end_seconds": 18.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Not great, I ended up a few streets away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.15,
      "end_seconds": 22.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "What made you decide to come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.61,
      "end_seconds": 36.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "Um, so... an itchy rash. That's why I came. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.04,
      "end_seconds": 38.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.37,
      "end_seconds": 46.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "About... well, four weeks. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.94,
      "end_seconds": 53.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.57,
      "end_seconds": 66.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.74,
      "text": "Uh, I'd say mild. I'd say all the time. I've never really been one for hospitals. I've also had cracked skin on my hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.49,
      "end_seconds": 69.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.78,
      "end_seconds": 84.87,
      "duration_seconds": 14.09,
      "text": "Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. I've also had itching that wakes me at night. With itching that wakes me at night, it's severe, honestly. There's redness as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.23,
      "end_seconds": 92.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Any breathing trouble or similar rash in family members at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.34,
      "end_seconds": 98.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "No breathing trouble or similar rash in family members, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.06,
      "end_seconds": 100.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "What about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.75,
      "end_seconds": 104.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "No, you know, I haven't had any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 106.0,
      "end_seconds": 110.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Uh, actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.15,
      "end_seconds": 118.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.58,
      "end_seconds": 126.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Have you had any joint pain, new soap or detergent or oozing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.17,
      "end_seconds": 129.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.39,
      "end_seconds": 133.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.57,
      "end_seconds": 137.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Okay, so no, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.33,
      "end_seconds": 141.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.93,
      "end_seconds": 143.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 144.32,
      "end_seconds": 156.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 69, weight 68 kilos, blood pressure 113 over 79, BMI works out to 27.6, height 157 centimetres, respiratory rate 14, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.14,
      "end_seconds": 161.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Thanks. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.06,
      "end_seconds": 165.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "My brother has asthma. My sister has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.7,
      "end_seconds": 180.43,
      "duration_seconds": 13.73,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.01,
      "end_seconds": 183.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.93,
      "end_seconds": 187.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.38,
      "end_seconds": 190.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Well, I had my gallbladder removed in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.85,
      "end_seconds": 193.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.21,
      "end_seconds": 197.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, um, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.02,
      "end_seconds": 213.6,
      "duration_seconds": 14.58,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.46,
      "end_seconds": 216.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.57,
      "end_seconds": 219.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 220.15,
      "end_seconds": 230.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.14,
      "text": "She is on Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma, I give it to her. She takes hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.78,
      "end_seconds": 233.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 234.53,
      "end_seconds": 236.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "For about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.6,
      "end_seconds": 241.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I see. Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.1,
      "end_seconds": 247.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Asthma, for nearly five years. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.98,
      "end_seconds": 250.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.89,
      "end_seconds": 258.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Eczema, for about a year. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.97,
      "end_seconds": 268.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "Okay, asthma, that's already on your record. Good to know. Right, so that's your known eczema. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.51,
      "end_seconds": 274.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.37,
      "end_seconds": 276.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.77,
      "end_seconds": 279.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.82,
      "end_seconds": 293.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "There are dry red patches in the creases of both elbows with scratch marks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.62,
      "end_seconds": 297.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.8,
      "end_seconds": 318.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "No signs of infection, no crusting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.4,
      "end_seconds": 345.4,
      "duration_seconds": 24.0,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like an eczema flare-up. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out contact dermatitis yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had an itchy rash for four weeks, mild, and no joint pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.61,
      "end_seconds": 348.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.4,
      "end_seconds": 360.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "I'm prescribing mometasone cream, once a day, for two weeks. That should help with eczema. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.47,
      "end_seconds": 362.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.55,
      "end_seconds": 391.27,
      "duration_seconds": 27.72,
      "text": "I'd like you to take cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for one week. You take it by mouth. That's for itching. Moisturise right after a bath, thick creams are better than lotions, and use a mild soap. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Please come and see me in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.53,
      "end_seconds": 396.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.6,
      "end_seconds": 406.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "So, I take the mometasone cream, once a day and take the cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.74,
      "end_seconds": 412.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.0,
      "end_seconds": 419.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}